---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
const crumbs = [{ name: "Privacy", path: "/privacy/" }];
---
<Base title="Reelbird privacy: no account needed, no telemetry" description="Recordings stay on your Mac. No analytics, no crash reporting, no update checks. Shares go to the bucket you configure, or to Reelbird Pro if you choose it." og="privacy" crumbs={crumbs}>
  <PageHead title="Privacy" lede="Reelbird needs no account. Your recordings stay on your Mac unless you share them, and then they go to storage you own, or to Reelbird Pro's hosting if you sign up for it." crumbs={crumbs} />
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose body">
      <h2 id="app">The app</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Recordings, edits, captions and transcripts stay on your Mac, in <code>~/Movies/Reelbird</code> unless you choose another folder.</li>
        <li>Find Sensitive Info reads the text on screen with Apple's on-device text recognition to suggest blurs. Nothing is uploaded, and the command line and MCP server show only masked previews of what it finds.</li>
        <li>Captions and titles are made on your Mac by Apple's frameworks. No API keys and no cloud services. On macOS 26, macOS downloads Apple's speech model the first time you make captions.</li>
        <li>Nothing is uploaded unless you share. With your own bucket, shares go only there, signed with your own keys. The secret key lives in your macOS Keychain and is only sent to your storage endpoint as a request signature.</li>
        <li>No analytics, no telemetry, no crash reporting and no update checks. The app only contacts the Reelbird server if you sign in to Reelbird Pro.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="links">Share links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Links are unlisted, not secret.</strong> Anyone who has a link can watch the video and forward the link. Random IDs make links impossible to guess, and the bucket isn't listable, but there's no password.</li>
        <li><strong>Sharing while recording uploads as you go.</strong> If you discard the take, Reelbird deletes everything it uploaded for it. That quick version has no edits, so blurs you add later reach viewers when you update the link.</li>
        <li><strong>Stop sharing</strong> deletes every file for that link. A CDN cache may serve a deleted file for a short time, and anyone who downloaded the video keeps their copy.</li>
        <li><strong>What viewers load.</strong> The viewer page, video and captions all come from your bucket. While a share has only the live stream, browsers without built-in HLS (Chrome, Firefox) also load the hls.js player from jsDelivr, pinned to one version and integrity-checked. Once you update the link, viewers get a plain MP4 and nothing else.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>More in <a href="/docs/sharing/#privacy">Sharing setup → Privacy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="pro">Reelbird Pro (optional)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your account</strong> is your email address. We use it to send sign-in links, nothing else. Signing in from the app gives it a token stored in your macOS Keychain.</li>
        <li><strong>Your shared videos</strong> are stored in Reelbird's private Cloudflare R2 bucket, under the link's random ID. Viewers get short-lived signed links to them. Deleting a link deletes its files.</li>
        <li><strong>Viewer analytics</strong> use no cookies. For each view we record how much of the video was watched, the referring site, the device type and browser, and the country when known. A viewer is counted with a daily hash of IP address and browser, so no IP address is stored and a person can't be followed across days or links.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments</strong> are handled by Stripe; we never see your card. We keep your Stripe customer ID and subscription status to know your plan.</li>
        <li>Cancel any time from your account page. Your links keep playing after Pro ends; delete them from the account page or the app.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="site">This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies and no advertising or cross-site trackers. Fonts and media are served from this site.</li>
        <li>We count visits with <a href="https://umami.is">Umami</a>, which we host ourselves. It sets no cookies, stores no IP addresses and records only the page, referrer, browser, device type and country. It never runs inside the Reelbird app.</li>
        <li>Your theme choice, if you pick one, is kept in your browser's local storage and never sent anywhere.</li>
        <li>The server that hosts this site may keep standard request logs (such as IP address, page and time) to keep it running.</li>
        <li>The Support page links to Stripe for payments. Stripe's own privacy policy applies there.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
      <p>Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/btahir/reelbird/issues">GitHub</a>. For a security problem, follow the repository's <a href="https://github.com/btahir/reelbird/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security policy</a>.</p>
      <p class="muted">Last updated 20 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .body { padding-bottom: var(--section); }
  .body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
</style>
